  "limitations": [
    "Final source supersedes draft 417bfd6f evidence; the final helper was rebuilt and all applicable native, race, probe, mutation, ledger and constrained-memory gates were repeated.",
    "Go SetMemoryLimit is soft and covers Go-managed memory, not total RSS; no OOM guarantee.",
    "Single measurements on a synthetic scanner corpus are functional evidence, not a throughput benchmark or general memory bound.",
    "The kernel exposes no memory.peak; group peaks are sampled every 5 ms. /usr/bin/time reports exact maximum process RSS.",
    "The 384 MiB baseline was OOM-killed and has no complete result; candidate completion is compared with complete baseline runs at larger caps.",
    "Earlier task-owned cgroups had mode 0700, making memory metadata unreadable after privilege drop. Their results exercise fallback only and are superseded by readable-cgroup runs; retained privately.",
    "A separate initial harness attempt assumed memory.peak existed and failed after its first measurement. Its empty owned namespace was verified and removed.",
